CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member of a class template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.closure]/1, [temp.spec.general]/1: the lambda in
size_of<C> has a distinct closure type, with its own call operator, in
size_of<char> and size_of<long long>.  The closure cache (lambda_closure_map)
was keyed on the parser's lambda number alone, which the specializations
share, so size_of<long long> reused size_of<char>'s closure and both calls
returned sizeof(char) (bin53).  The key now includes the enclosing scope.
In libstdc++'s <format> the wchar_t _Formatting_scanner used the char
scanner's visitor closure, and basic_format_arg::_M_visit and the
visitor's operator() were dropped.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
